  "Setup helper reach table. Hand-made: edit freely, no code change needed.",
  "controls: one entry per built-in control id (both VKB Gladiator NXT EVO sticks; they share ids except the mini-stick and red button).",
  "  rank: 1 = easiest to reach with the hand on the grip, 10 = hardest. zone: thumb / index / pinky / base (shown in the plan).",
  "  centering (axes only): spring = springs back to centre, free = stays where you leave it (absolute).",
  "  Controls not listed here (ones you mapped yourself) count as rank 10.",
  "main_axes: the stick's own axes by SC name (x, y, z, rotx, roty, rotz, slider1, slider2) for each kind of stick.",
  "  spring = a normal spring-centred stick, omni = VKB Omni throttle adapter (forward/back no longer springs back).",
  "  An axis not listed is spring-centred.",
  "weights: how a placement is scored (lower is better). A control's reach r runs 0 (rank 1) to 1 (rank 10).",
  "  use_targets: the r each kind of action wants (often = best reach, rare = the base buttons).",
  "  displace: cost per bind it would replace (same mode). share: cost per bind kept there in another mode (on foot + flight is fine).",
  "  sequence_bonus: per action, how much worse the reach on one hat may be before the helper spreads a sequence out instead.",
  "  hat_order: which hat directions a sequence fills, in order."
